  "body": "Estimated end-of-life date, accurate to within three months: 05-2027\r\nSee [the support level definitions](https://docs.datadoghq.com/tracing/trace_collection/compatibility/python/#releases) for more information.\r\n\r\n## v4.16.4\r\n\r\n### Bug Fixes\r\n\r\n- profiling\r\n  - Fixes a crash that can happen when a uWSGI process exits while the stack profiler is running, for example a worker started with `--lazy-apps --skip-atexit` or a `--master` process with `--py-call-uwsgi-fork-hooks`.\r\n  - Fixes a crash with `failed to intern string: OutOfMemory` when the process runs out of memory while the profiler exports a profile. The profile is now dropped instead.\r\n- uWSGI\r\n  - Fixes an issue where uWSGI workers can hang at startup when `ddtrace` is imported in the master process and neither `lazy-apps` nor `py-call-uwsgi-fork-hooks` is set.\r\n"
